# Spring Modulith Test Dependency (Maven)

Generated by arbiter (#1886). `ApplicationModulesTest.java` imports
`org.springframework.modulith.core.ApplicationModules`, which is not on the
classpath by default — add this dependency to your `pom.xml` under
`<dependencies>` or the build will fail to compile.

Pinned to the Spring Modulith 1.4.x line, which targets Spring Boot 3.x / Spring
Framework 6 (Spring Modulith 2.x requires Spring Boot 4 / Framework 7 — see
https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-modulith/issues/971). If your project
is on Spring Boot 4, use the matching 2.x version instead.

```xml
<!-- Spring Modulith — structural module verification (ApplicationModules.verify()) -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.modulith</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-modulith-starter-test</artifactId>
    <version>1.4.12</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
```
